  "verbalization": "Stipuleanoside R2 is implicated in the biological activity of FaDu through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Stipuleanoside R2 directly targets SK-OV-3, a cell line that is subsequently targeted by Glaucolide B and 3alpha-Hydroxy-6beta-tigloyloxytropane. These compounds, in turn, target FaDu, indicating a chain of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the effect on FaDu. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, with overlapping targets and a clear hierarchical structure in the pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a potential mechanism where Stipuleanoside R2 influences SK-OV-3, which then acts on FaDu, suggesting a possible role in the biological response of this cell line. The evidence supports a direct or indirect link between Stipuleanoside R2 and FaDu through a series of molecular targets, reinforcing the notion of a functional relationship in the context of the dataset.",
